<div class="<%= placement %>">
  <%#
    Everything true *about* the post, on one line. It is a measurement, so it
    is mono; it is not the writing, so it is one step below it in value and it
    sits under the title rather than over it — a reader who just tapped a
    headline meets the thing they opened, not its machinery.
  %>
  <dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1 font-mono text-meta text-mauve-11">
    <div>
      <dt class="sr-only">Published</dt>

      <dd class="m-0">
        <time datetime="<%= date.iso8601 %>"><%= date.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %></time>
      </dd>
    </div>

    <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-mauve-9">·</span>

    <div>
      <dt class="sr-only">Reading time</dt>
      <dd class="m-0"><%= reading_time %> min read</dd>
    </div>

    <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-mauve-9">·</span>

    <div>
      <dt class="sr-only">Author</dt>

      <dd class="m-0">
        <a
          href="/about/"
          rel="author"
          class="inline-block py-1 -my-1 underline decoration-mauve-7 underline-offset-4 hover:text-mauve-12 hover:decoration-ruby-11 transition-colors"
        ><%= author_name %></a>
      </dd>
    </div>

    <% if tags.any? %>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-mauve-9">·</span>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
        <dt class="sr-only">Tags</dt>

        <% tags.each do |tag| %>
          <dd class="m-0">
            <%= render Link.new(href: "/tag/#{tag}/", variant: :post_tag) do %>
              #<%= tag %>
            <% end %>
          </dd>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>

  <% if show_toc? %>
    <%#
      Filled at build time by Builders::Inspectors::Toc, which reads the real
      rendered headings rather than guessing from source markdown — so the
      entries agree with the anchor IDs the reader actually lands on.

      A disclosure at every width now, rather than a rail on desktop and a
      disclosure on a phone: the pane has no margin to hang a rail in, and one
      rendering that behaves identically everywhere is one behaviour to get
      right. The chevron is the affordance and it rotates from the open state
      in CSS rather than from JS.
    %>
    <details data-toc-wrap class="group mt-6" hidden>
      <summary
        class="
          list-none marker:hidden cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center gap-2
          rounded-md -mx-2 px-2 py-1 font-mono text-label text-mauve-11
          hover:bg-mauve-3 hover:text-mauve-12 transition-colors
        "
      >
        <%= render Icon.new(
          name: "chevron_right",
          class: "w-3.5 h-3.5 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-90",
        ) %>
        contents
      </summary>

      <nav data-toc aria-label="Contents" class="mt-3"></nav>
    </details>
  <% end %>
</div>
